# FINAL DIRECTIVE

Do not approach Aetheria as a collection of features that needs to become larger.

Approach it as a world that needs to become more believable, an adventure that needs to become more compelling and a game that needs to become more enjoyable.

Aetheria should offer the excitement of an extraordinary fantasy adventure while giving players the freedom to create their own experiences within it.

The player should care about the people they meet.

They should remember the places they visit.

They should be excited to discover new abilities.

They should recognise monsters by their behaviour.

They should feel the weight of their decisions.

They should have reasons to return to places they have already visited.

They should feel that their companions are travelling with them, not merely following them.

They should experience the satisfaction of becoming powerful without losing the sense of wonder that made the beginning special.

Most importantly, every major system should contribute to a coherent experience.

**Build a world worth getting lost in. Build characters worth remembering. Build combat worth mastering. Build an adventure worth completing.**

